// @ens-test
// @exit 1
// @stdout-contains PASS first test passes
// @stdout-contains The test run ended unexpectedly
// @stdout-contains while running test 'second test panics'
// @stdout-contains crash_test.ens
// @stdout-contains 1 of 2 tests had reported a result
// A panic in the second test aborts the whole run. The first result still
// survives (it was flushed), and the report names the test that was running
// when the run ended plus how many results came before it. The panic's own
// message goes to the child's stderr, which the harness redirects onto the same
// file as stdout with a separate write cursor; that clobbers the earliest bytes,
// so this fixture asserts only on output that survives that merge.
